{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790329886,"nonce":"+89JRGkgko8FmHfB+zgHfNsYO3Y=","message":"User decisions (2026-09-25):\n- Windows: forwarder DLLs (python3.dll, python3XY.dll; lua54.dll for the Lua C API) placed next to the executable are allowed. They carry no API code and forward every export to the executable.\n- The repository may vendor CPython's Include/ trees (PSF-2.0, with its notice) and CPython's pure-Python Lib sources, compiled by zypy for numpy's import chain. The C API and the C accelerators (_sre, _ast, ...) are written fresh.\n- Packages come from pip-filled CPython venvs (VIRTUAL_ENV, pyvenv.cfg, ZYPY_PATH); no installer of zypy's own.\n- Concurrency: free-threaded CPython (cp3XYt) shares one heap between threads and is not an isolate model, so it stays refused. Phase 7 becomes subinterpreters (PEP 684 per-interpreter GIL, PEP 734 concurrent.interpreters) on an isolate model: one zypy runtime per thread with its own heap and scheduler, values crossing by copy and queues, standard GIL-ABI wheels that declare per-module state. Proposed to the user, following their pointer to an isolate design; free-threaded wheels are revisited only if the runtime ever needs shared-memory mutators.","files":null}]}